[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Fluorita
GenericName=Reproductor multimedia
Comment=Reproduce y organiza tu música, tus vídeos y tus imágenes
Exec=fluorita %f
Icon=org.celestina.Fluorita
Terminal=false
Categories=AudioVideo;Player;Video;Audio;
Keywords=música;vídeo;imagen;reproductor;fluorita;celestina;music;video;player;
StartupNotify=true
StartupWMClass=org.celestina.Fluorita
# `%f`, not `%F`: this player opens one item, and a launcher that handed it a
# whole selection would silently drop everything after the first.
#
# This list puts Fluorita in "Abrir con" — and, where the user has expressed no
# preference of their own, it also makes Fluorita what the desktop opens: with
# nothing pinned in `mimeapps.list`, being registered is what decides. Measured
# rather than assumed: installing moved video/mp4, mkv, webm, quicktime,
# audio/flac, ogg, wav and image/webp from VLC and other viewers to this entry.
# The author accepted that on 2026-07-31; anyone who wants it otherwise pins the
# application they prefer, which always wins over this list.
#
# What a file *is* stays decided elsewhere: by `fluorita-core` from the name and
# by the engine from the bytes. This list never decides whether something can be
# played.
MimeType=audio/mpeg;audio/flac;audio/ogg;audio/opus;audio/x-vorbis+ogg;audio/wav;audio/x-wav;audio/mp4;audio/aac;audio/x-ms-wma;audio/x-aiff;audio/x-ape;audio/x-wavpack;audio/x-matroska;video/mp4;video/x-matroska;video/webm;video/quicktime;video/x-msvideo;video/x-ms-wmv;video/x-flv;video/mpeg;video/mp2t;video/ogg;video/3gpp;image/png;image/jpeg;image/gif;image/webp;image/bmp;image/tiff;image/avif;image/jxl;image/heif;
